From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 03:38:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: unify queue speed for DSA and non-DSA

mtk_device_event() only walked DSA conduit/user pairs and bailed early
on non-DSA netdev change events, so direct GMACs (e.g. mt7987 GMAC1)
never had a per-queue rate cap programmed.

Match the DSA path: when the event is for the mac's own netdev, use
queue = mac->id. Skip bridge upper events to avoid double-processing.

Keep the upstream bottleneck guard (commit e669ce46740a "net: ethernet:
mtk_eth_soc: fix remaining throughput regression") in place for both
paths: when the GMAC link itself is the bottleneck, shaping at the MAC
rate is redundant and lossy, so leave the queue uncapped. Direct GMACs
behind interface-switching PHYs (GPY211, MXL86211C) run the MAC at
line speed and thus stay uncapped; rate-matching USXGMII PHYs keep the
MAC above line speed and retain the cap.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c |   27 +++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3900,33 +3900,40 @@ static int mtk_device_event(struct notif
 	struct dsa_port *dp;
 	unsigned int queue;
 
-	if (event != NETDEV_CHANGE)
+	if (event != NETDEV_CHANGE || dev->priv_flags & IFF_EBRIDGE)
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
+	/* DSA conduit event: dev is a DSA user port stacked on this mac. */
 	netdev_for_each_lower_dev(dev, ldev, iter) {
 		if (netdev_priv(ldev) == mac)
 			goto found;
 	}
 
+	/* Direct GMAC event: dev itself is the mac's netdev. */
+	if (netdev_priv(dev) == mac)
+		goto found;
+
 	return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
 found:
-	if (!dsa_user_dev_check(dev))
-		return NOTIFY_DONE;
-
-	mtk_update_dsa_queue_map(eth);
-
 	if (__ethtool_get_link_ksettings(dev, &s))
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
 	if (s.base.speed == 0 || s.base.speed == ((__u32)-1))
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
-	dp = dsa_port_from_netdev(dev);
-	if (dp->index >= MTK_DSA_USER_PORT_MAX)
-		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+	if (dsa_user_dev_check(dev)) {
+		mtk_update_dsa_queue_map(eth);
+
+		dp = dsa_port_from_netdev(dev);
+		if (dp->index >= MTK_DSA_USER_PORT_MAX)
+			return NOTIFY_DONE;
+
+		queue = mac->dsa_queue_base + mac->dsa_port_rank[dp->index];
+	} else {
+		queue = mac->id;
+	}
 
-	queue = mac->dsa_queue_base + mac->dsa_port_rank[dp->index];
 	if (queue >= eth->soc->num_tx_queues)
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 
